+// ─── Gcollision-wallslide fix: host-pointer mips2c->GOALC symbol return ──────
+// `(method 9/10 collide-puss-work)` return the GOAL symbol #t/#f to the GOALC
+// caller `probe-using-spheres`, which tests it with `(when v1-12 (return #t))`.
+// On arm64 GOALC materialises the #f it compares against as the symbol-table
+// register — a HOST pointer, g_ee_main_mem + offset (IR.cpp IR_LoadSymbolPointer
+// do_codegen_arm64: `#f` -> get_st_reg()). But the mips2c VM stores symbols as
+// BARE 32-bit offsets (mips2c_private.h:311: addr - g_ee_main_mem), so these
+// leaves return #f as a bare offset whose upper-32 is zero. GOALC's 64-bit
+// `(when v1-12)` compare then reads bare-offset-#f != host-pointer-#f as
+// "not false" -> `fill-and-probe-using-spheres` wrongly reports a blocking head
+// sphere -> `can-exit-duck?` returns #f and Jak is stuck PERMANENTLY crouched at
+// certain Geyser-Rock walls even with no input (owner defect; x86, whose GOAL
+// pointers fit a single 32-bit model, is unaffected). The leaf's per-triangle
+// hit/miss math is itself bit-identical to x86 — only the boolean RETURN pointer
+// representation diverges (the documented arm64 #f-guard / pointer-representation
+// class; cf. the per-site gpr_addr fixes elsewhere in this file, which fix the
+// COMPARE side; this fixes the RETURN side). Re-tag the #t/#f offset as the host
+// pointer GOALC expects. arm64-only; on x86 the return is left untouched.
+static inline u64 gpuss_canonical_symbol_return(u64 ret) {
+#if defined(__aarch64__)
+  return (u64)(uintptr_t)g_ee_main_mem + (u32)ret;
+#else
+  return ret;
+#endif
+}
